Replace vector-similarity-search stub with real pgvector implementation (#903)

Original task: replace the empty `vector-similarity-search` Edge Function
stub with a real handler that runs a pgvector similarity query and returns
ranked, enriched matches the recommendation engine can render.

Changes
- supabase/functions/vector-similarity-search/index.ts: rewritten from a
  stub returning `{ matches: [], stub: true }` into a real handler. It now:
    * Accepts EITHER `query_embedding` (must be 1536-dim, the canonical
      EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS used by `vector-embed`) OR `query_text`, which
      it embeds server-side via the shared `generateEmbedding` adapter.
      This fixes the dimension mismatch between the in-browser
      recommendation engine (which builds 128-dim simulated vectors) and
      the pgvector columns (1536-dim).
    * Validates inputs (finite numeric array, length, threshold range,
      capped match_count).
    * Calls the existing `match_embeddings(p_table_name, p_query_embedding,
      p_match_threshold, p_match_count)` RPC for `listings`,
      `marketplace_services`, and `seed_products` in parallel.
    * Enriches matches with title/image/subtitle from each table using a
      single `IN (...)` query per table; merges, sorts by similarity desc,
      and truncates to match_count.
    * Degrades gracefully (per-table errors don't fail the whole call)
      and removes the `stub: true` marker.
- src/engines/recommendations/recommendation-engine.ts: `fetchPgvectorSimilar`
  now sends `query_text` derived from the user's recent verticals and
  favorited catalog titles instead of the local 128-dim simulated vector,
  so the request actually returns ranked matches.
- supabase/functions/_contracts.ts: updated request/response/error schema
  to reflect optional `query_embedding | query_text` and the new 502 path.
- supabase/functions/_manifest.ts: rate-limit `reason` no longer says
  "Stub function".

Notes / deviations
- Did not consolidate into `vector-embed` / `ai-router` (that is the larger
  #226 effort). The function uses the same shared embedding-client.ts so
  consolidation later is straightforward.
- Existing rows likely have NULL embeddings until the embedding backfill
  runs (see follow-up #919), so user-visible results depend on backfill.
  The query path itself is fully real.

Follow-ups proposed: #919 (backfill embeddings), #920 (tests).

